# Fixed defect 133, 2026-09-29. Symptom: `struct Point {` cost
# `reserved_word` alone, and only once `check --apply` had written
# `record Point {` did the next run report `empty_record`; a field missing
# its colon under `struct` waited the same way. Cause: the lexer emits the
# refused word as an `error` token, and at a top-level line's head the
# parser's recovery dropped the whole declaration with its fields. The
# parser now reads `struct`, whose certain swap is `record`, as `record`
# (`parse/swap_reading.hero`). The `}` is refused as it is after the swap.
# A record with no fields above a `struct` line is empty all the same: the
# guard that stayed silent at the lexer's `error` token reads the next
# line's head as its swap, `record`, and says so.
#
# Moved the same day, a second round (defect 131's class): `struct Point {`
# over its fields is the brace habit, one mistake. Its `{` is the head's junk,
# named as such with where the fields go, `expected_end_of_line`, where it
# was `empty_record`, which said the fields were missing while they stood in
# the braces; and the `}` that closes them is the habit's debris, no longer
# `expected_declaration`.

record Size
    w: i64

record Point {  #~ reserved_word expected_end_of_line
    x: i64
}

record Pair  #~ reserved_word
    left i64  #~ expected_field_type
    right: i64

record Nothing  #~ empty_record

record Whole  #~ reserved_word
    x: i64

function main()
    print(1)
